{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/857464-punishment-rights-and-you","id":857464,"title":"Punishment rights and you!","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-04-01T21:11:38-07:00","id":857464,"title":"Punishment rights and you!","content":"So, what's to stop someone handing out punishment rights willy-nilly, because mechanically you can do it to anyone.<br /> <br /> Say the swords of heimdall (The worst racists of fenrir) come across a female black lupus get that might even have some fera blood in them. Can they just perform punishment on such a character? Rite of renunciation, stone of scorn, even gaia's vengeful teeth... The character has done nothing wrong, but they believe themselves to be in the right, and a skilled ritesmaster is a skilled ritesmaster.<br /> <br /> Alternatively, a shadowlord has a rival. He knocks his rival down a peg with punishment rites. His enemy decreased in honour and rank is now a lesser threat to him.<br /> Lastly, with the shadowlord, he can engineer his rival into the position for a punishment rite (framing or just being put into unwinnable situations) Would this affect rites?<br /> <br /> <br /> Also I've theorized that if Gaia's teeth should be survivalable. The question being; How long does it last. Infinite? well, of course 'nobody survives this rite' applies, if it's infinite. A month? Difficult. A week? Doable, less? Very possible, all depending on what gifts you've got. If you're a ragabash or gnawer or silent strider or uktena you'll maybe have some tricky gift that'll outpace the pack without causing you to burn against too many things. (we can debate on metaphysics and the occult when it comes to <i>luna's blessing</i>, but <i>Great Leap</i> alone is an excellent escape tool. There are many other gifts and possibly fetishes which would be of great value here.)<br /> Like, yeah, sure, if you're fantastic at escaping you likely wouldn't have been around long enough to be subjected to the rite in the first place, but that unlucky character or particularly daring trickster might attempt a post-rite escape (the point of the rite is the humiliating chase, after all, might as well utilize that in knocking low some pride)<br /> <br /> I argued this with a friend, he got very mad. Apparently, the point of the rite is that the recipient dies, and you can't survive it. I feel like that really takes the cleverness out of it. If a player is clever enough to escape, they you shouldn't railroad them to death, Escaping is worth massive renown (possibly counterballanced by whatever they did to be victim anyhow) and they will no doubt will feel awesome about it. If a ritesmaster goes through the trouble to use this rite and it doesn't result in a dead victim, then they're a fool for not simply executing the offender outright.<br /> <br /> Now the <i>rite of hell made flesh</i>, there's a fun one to figure out how to escape from.<br /> (i've already got ideas)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":7244,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7244-innocent-flower","user":"Innocent Flower","date":". 04-02-2016, 01:06 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7244-innocent-flower","name":"Innocent Flower","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7244_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"322"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-01T21:36:47-07:00","id":857481,"title":"","content":"I can see why your friend got very mad at you. Does this happen often why you bring up things that break the game if you don't apply common sense to them?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-01T23:42:16-07:00","id":857539,"title":"","content":"Minor nitpick: you can't force Renunciation on someone. It's an Accord Rite and has to be performed by the Garou seeking to change Auspices.<br /> <br /> In general though, the Punishment Rites section is pretty clear that the ST is free to have such rites fail if used without cause (and even backfire to cause those trying to use them against their intended purposes) specifically to stop any such shenanigans. This is actually a quote from the general system section for Punishment Rites from W20: &quot;Because these rites are enforced and empowered by the spirit world, truly unjust punishment rites may fail automatically, leading to a sure loss of Honor for the one who ordered them.&quot;<br /> <br /> So no, you can't just use them willy-nilly; or rather you can, but you're just going to lose Honor like mad for abusing your authority while the subject doesn't suffer any repercussions.<br /> <br /> It doesn't matter what the Ritemaster and any helpers believe. It matters what the spirits <i>know</i>, and if they know the use of the Rite isn't just, they'll refuse to empower it.<br /> <br /> As for Gaia's Vengeful Teeth, I wouldn't really take the text to mean that the Rite itself causes death. It has a set end condition for its effects. Surviving it is impossible more because at least six Garou have you subdued well enough to perform the Rite, and are now trying to actively kill you once the Rtemaster is done.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-02T02:24:05-07:00","id":857589,"title":"","content":"Honestly, nothing short of Uncaught Since the Primal Morn would delay death more than a few minutes, and that is if the Garou has a reliable way to soak silver damage. Garou are excellent hunters already, and those who performed the rite are not likely to give the wretch much of a head start.<br /> <br /> As Heavy Arms mentioned, Garou justice is supposed to be quite reliable (if not 'fair'). Under what possible circumstanced would lead to a corrupt Philodox unjustly enacting such a rite? As a GM, if you are using this rite, if a player is subject to Gaia's Vengeful Teeth, they probably should stop being a player character at all, since they have fucked up royal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-02T06:14:38-07:00","id":857655,"title":"","content":"<b>Gaia\u2019s Vengeful Teeth</b><br /> Level Five<br /> As one of the greatest punishments among the Garou,<br /> this rite is reserved for traitors, those who consort with<br /> the Wyrm or cowards whose actions (or lack thereof)<br /> cause the deaths of many others. At least five werewolves<br /> drag the traitor to a spot of hard, cracked earth and<br /> stones. The ritemaster then stabs a sharpened twig or<br /> stone into her own hand as she recites the traitor\u2019s sins<br /> against Gaia. Smearing her blood over the traitor\u2019s eyes,<br /> ears and forehead, the ritemaster cries in grief and rage.<br /> As the blood and tears drip to the hard ground, the rite<br /> takes effect. From that moment on, whatever of Gaia<br /> touches the traitor transforms into razor-sharp silver so<br /> long as it touches his flesh. Crinos hunters then chase<br /> the traitor like a dog. The ground beneath the traitor<br /> chews into his feet, and his death becomes an agonizing<br /> ordeal. The offender\u2019s name is then stricken from<br /> all histories, and it will be spoken only as a curse from<br /> that moment forward.<br /> <b>System</b>: As long as the ritemaster\u2019s blood touches<br /> the traitor\u2019s body, the traitor cannot step sideways into<br /> the Umbra. No one survives being subject to this rite.<br /> <br /> <br /> From that moment on, whatever of Gaia touches the traitor transforms into razor-sharp silver so long as it touches his flesh. Good luck using Hare's leap ( or other variations) that landing is going to hurt, the pain is going to drive the victim to frenzy very quickly. It is possible to wash the blood off but there are still at least five garou in pursuit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11552-molono","name":"molono","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-02T10:51:58-07:00","id":857798,"title":"","content":"I believe Punishment Rites can only be approved as a result of the sept's decisions during Moots, specifically the Cracking of the Bone. If a Garou accuses another Garou of violating the Litany (as interpreted by that sept there), the sept judges it and pronounces justice according to sept tradition. That punishment can include one of the Punishment Rites. At that point, a Garou who knows that Rite will perform it on behalf of the sept.<br /> <br /> I don't believe the kind of vigilant justice (more like injustice) is permitted within Garou society. Of course, if you perform the Rites the Rites still work. But once word gets out that this is being done, the Garou of the local septs will begin hunting down the perpetrators. When they find them, they'll judge and punish them. In addition, for any Garou who was unjustly punished, their local sept will take the necessary steps to &quot;reverse&quot; the Punishment Rite innflicted upon them.<br /> <br /> So what's to stop someone handing them out willy nilly? Garou society itself. A person who does so will be driven into exile from the nation, if not killed outright. He will be stripped of Renown and may even become Ronin. The behavior you described is like a Judge deciding to form a star chamber and hiring someone to perform extrajudicial executions. No matter how much he justifies it, his actions are completely illegal and have no force of law. He is engaged in criminal acts himself.<br /> <br /> Frankly, someone who even seems like he intends to do such things will never be allowed to learn such Rites in the first place.<br /> <br /> And if there is even a sept of such Garou who do such things, the other local septs will likely judge them to be of the Wyrm and go to war with the intent on destroying them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-02T12:37:09-07:00","id":857856,"title":"","content":"A ST can &quot;Auto Fail&quot; Any punishment rite performed for an unjust cause.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-02T15:40:46-07:00","id":857967,"title":"","content":"<br /> You could arguably escape Gaia's teeth with<br /> The gifts Great leap, spirit of the bird and/or Patagia. <br /> Speed of thought or speed beyond thought (will likely need willpower rolls to stay standing, or some protection) <br /> Luna's blessing<br /> Luna's avenger<br /> The marriage of sun and moon. <br /> Shadowstep <br /> One of the hundred stealth gifts, or many of the social domination gifts. <br /> <br /> to name a few.But it really depends on how long the rite lasts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7244-innocent-flower","name":"Innocent Flower","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7244_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"322"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-02T15:51:52-07:00","id":857970,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Innocent Flower</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/857464-punishment-rights-and-you?p=857967#post857967\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You could arguably escape Gaia's teeth with<br /> The gifts Great leap, spirit of the bird and/or Patagia. <br /> Speed of thought or speed beyond thought (will likely need willpower rolls to stay standing, or some protection) <br /> Luna's blessing<br /> Luna's avenger<br /> The marriage of sun and moon. <br /> Shadowstep <br /> One of the hundred stealth gifts, or many of the social domination gifts. <br /> <br /> to name a few.But it really depends on how long the rite lasts.</div> </div> </div> </div>Except for that whole, everything you touch is razors of silver, hunted by probably an entire sept and the unending part, you know totally survivable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-02T16:22:56-07:00","id":857991,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>molono</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/857464-punishment-rights-and-you?p=857655#post857655\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Gaia\u2019s Vengeful Teeth</b><br /> <br /> <b>System</b>: As long as the ritemaster\u2019s blood touches<br /> the traitor\u2019s body, the traitor cannot step sideways into<br /> the Umbra. <b>No one survives being subject to this rite.</b><br /></div> </div> </div> </div>The highlighted part sums it up. Its not &quot;difficult&quot; or &quot;near impossible&quot; or &quot;no one yet&quot; it's specifically no one. The theme of the rite is that the silver doesn't end (your gnosis and sanity will) and as a GM I wouldn't allow gifts like Luna's Avenger to activate since the point of the rite is a guaranteed death. I know it may not state that specifically but as a GM that would be a result of the rite in my games. Granted in my games if you do something to deserve that rite, I personally feel you forfeited all rights to have a shot at survival. It's no minor mess up....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1179-celtspz","name":"CeltSPZ","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1179_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"835"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-02T17:40:01-07:00","id":858030,"title":"","content":"But is the point of the right a garanteed death? is having the point of a rite being garanteed death suffecient enough to garantee death?<br /> <br /> Firstly, the main point isn't to kill someone. If it was, it'd be horribly ineffecient. The point is to humiliate someone to the very bottom and making an ultimate example to the pack which kills them, and the rite's magic encourages the pack to be successful. The point of the rite is not the death, the rite doesn't bring death. The pack brings death. But if the pack is ineffective....<br /> <br /> You're asking a lot from a rite. This isn't supposed to be some kind of Pen and paper's mechanical termination/extended death scene, this is a magical ability, and magic is not meant to be flawless- Everything touched turns to silver (probably with the exception of dedicated items) No stepping sideways, and this works for all time? Plus you guys are saying gifts shouldn't work? And the rite should always result in death?<br /> <br /> Also, if someone survived the rite, would anyone write about it? That'd be a gigantic embarrassment for the garou. You'd hush it up. The point of the lesson is 'we'll give you the most horrific and inglorious experience if you fuck up this bad&quot; You're not going to tell the claith about that time znegrazah the child-raping wyrm-garou tricked the good and honourable Morningkill philidox into giving him a punishment he could escape, right? Nobody want's to hear the glorious escape of znegrazah, it really undermines garou justice.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7244-innocent-flower","name":"Innocent Flower","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7244_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"322"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-02T17:48:28-07:00","id":858037,"title":"","content":"It's not humiliation, it's to show the slow, painful death that awaits traitors. <br /> <br /> Plus your starting to sound like a troll.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-02T17:52:27-07:00","id":858041,"title":"","content":"The &quot;No one survives&quot; is not in the fluff, it's not in the oral stories, it's flat out in the system. The system states no one survives. Its a method of execution, so yes it's main point is in fact death, a terrible death meant to leave a message but it's end result is death. The WoD games are famous for their not covering or thinking about every little contingency that can occur (such as all the gifts you list). So it's rather neat and clean for a WoD game by saying &quot;no one survives&quot; (again not &quot;it is said no one survives&quot;). If you disagree with my reading into the rite that such gifts wouldn't work, that's fine. It does however state &quot;no one survives&quot; so there is no reason to believe that the effect of things turning to silver would eventually end before the subject dies. You may think this is a lot to ask from a rite but also keep in mind it's a level 5 rite. These are the highest rites the Garou have (I only know of a single lvl 6 rite and it was a Fianna rite that let you sleep like King Arthur, I was not impressed), so I don't see why its expecting a lot.<br /> <br /> Also if the point of a rite is to guarantee death, yes that's sufficient enough to guarantee death.<br /> <br /> Also, you can rule it anyway you want at your table. But the consensus seems to be that if you're looking for support here at these forums, you may not find what you seek.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1179,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1179-celtspz","user":"CeltSPZ","date":". 04-02-2016, 08:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1179-celtspz","name":"CeltSPZ","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1179_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"835"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-02T19:05:22-07:00","id":858077,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CeltSPZ</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/857464-punishment-rights-and-you?p=858041#post858041\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The &quot;No one survives&quot; is not in the fluff, it's not in the oral stories, it's flat out in the system. The system states no one survives. Its a method of execution, so yes it's main point is in fact death, a terrible death meant to leave a message but it's end result is death. The WoD games are famous for their not covering or thinking about every little contingency that can occur (such as all the gifts you list). So it's rather neat and clean for a WoD game by saying &quot;no one survives&quot; (again not &quot;it is said no one survives&quot;). If you disagree with my reading into the rite that such gifts wouldn't work, that's fine. It does however state &quot;no one survives&quot; so there is no reason to believe that the effect of things turning to silver would eventually end before the subject dies. You may think this is a lot to ask from a rite but also keep in mind it's a level 5 rite. These are the highest rites the Garou have (<b>I only know of a single lvl 6 rite and it was a Fianna rite that let you sleep like King Arthur, I was not impressed</b>), so I don't see why its expecting a lot.<br /> <br /> Also if the point of a rite is to guarantee death, yes that's sufficient enough to guarantee death.<br /> <br /> Also, you can rule it anyway you want at your table. But the consensus seems to be that if you're looking for support here at these forums, you may not find what you seek.</div> </div> </div> </div>There was one in Croatan Song that allowed the participants to raise the sun at night.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-02T19:37:36-07:00","id":858093,"title":"","content":"Forgot about that one...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1179-celtspz","name":"CeltSPZ","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1179_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"835"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-03T04:59:11-07:00","id":858276,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/857464-punishment-rights-and-you?p=858077#post858077\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There was one in Croatan Song that allowed the participants to raise the sun at night.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh I forgot that one. And here I thought the Mokole were the nastiest enemies of the Vamps :P","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-03T07:39:07-07:00","id":858335,"title":"","content":"Seriously doubt things like Great Leap and Patagaia would help, or any of the Stealth Gifts as you'll be taking Silver Damage every turn from the moment the Rite Concludes. &quot;But I can Fly!&quot; I hear you cry, that's great, the AIR is something of Gaia. So of you really want to break it down there would be a Damage Roll for Moving and a Damage Roll for Breathing as you suck silver razors into your lungs. Thats also going to be a Frenzy check everything that silver hits you. So good luck staying hidden.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2767-moirdryd","name":"Moirdryd","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2767_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-03T10:08:05-07:00","id":858388,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moirdryd</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/857464-punishment-rights-and-you?p=858335#post858335\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Seriously doubt things like Great Leap and Patagaia would help, or any of the Stealth Gifts as you'll be taking Silver Damage every turn from the moment the Rite Concludes. &quot;But I can Fly!&quot; I hear you cry, that's great, the AIR is something of Gaia. So of you really want to break it down there would be a Damage Roll for Moving and a Damage Roll for Breathing as you suck silver razors into your lungs. Thats also going to be a Frenzy check everything that silver hits you. So good luck staying hidden.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Also really true, too often we think of Gaia as just the earth and what grows off of it. Werewolf has her as everything natural, I didn't even stop and think about the air surrounding you and filling your lungs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1179-celtspz","name":"CeltSPZ","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1179_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"835"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-03T10:54:36-07:00","id":858401,"title":"","content":"Personally, a misguided philodox using these rites and them backfiring/failing could offer a lot of good story beats if done correctly.<br /> <br /> But yes, these are rituals of punishments, they cannot be used willy nilly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-04T06:14:52-07:00","id":858939,"title":"","content":"Hey All.<br /> <br /> You mention lot of fancy stuff to avoid greasy fate if punished by GVT: Flying, jumping around like a cricket, etc.<br /> <br /> I think you forgot something: The tiny particles in the air, your fallen of hair, your split saliva, your sweat, your crust of skin, your teardrops &amp; may even your outflowing blood will became silver splinters / thorns / blades etc. (They left your body &amp; not a part of it, but contact it.)<br /> <br /> Imagine that fate &amp; try to evade it somehow.<br /> <br /> And there is 2 other rite in the Apocalypse, the Vengeful Spider &amp; Awakening the Monn (or something like that), which is level 6.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/562-lachdanan","name":"Lachdanan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar562_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-04T06:40:29-07:00","id":858954,"title":"","content":"Martin, the new Lead Storyteller at White Wolf, recently said something about the WoD being realistic in contrast to fantasy settings. While wondering how Mage and Changeling would be non-fantastic, I think it going a bit far if one attributes the Rites to-silver-transmutation property to air or bodily emanations.<br /> <br /> The transmutation should affect, imo, solid objects that make physical contact with the garou's body. If it was to also be applied to liquids, the garou would die of dehydration really fast. Then again, the Rite should be deadly within moments, so not being able to drink would be a problem not worth mentioning. But having the insides of one's lungs coated with silver would lead to asphyxiation so quickly, that it would be mentioned in the Rite's write-up if the Rite would work that way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1008,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","user":"heinrich","date":". 04-04-2016, 09:43 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-04T07:38:25-07:00","id":858992,"title":"","content":"I think it's a really poorly worded rite. <br /> By saying 'you should be able to survive it' I'm not saying 'players should be bad because they can escape punishment'. I just think a flawless rite is, well, not interesting. It really get's in the way of all the treasonous ideas one could have.<br /> <br /> IE The ritesmaster secretly doesn't want the offender to die, so opts to use the brutal 'maybe' right than the perfect 'sure death' rite. There are tons of reasons why the ritemaster could possibly not want the offender to die. He could be corrupt himself, He could want to have the traitor lure the characters to the main badguy, or the rite could be used to take suspicion from the offender, who's really a loyal gaian spy. <br /> <br /> The players came up with some genius unbeatable plan/got really lucky rolls the storyteller didn't forsee, and you just can't bullshit to nullify a good plan, but you also don't want a great story arc gone in half a session. So you have an NPC want to capture the target, and then gaia's vengeful teeth is used, which is escaped from. <br /> <br /> Also, I think it'd just be a really good way to introduce an antagonist, to have him survive something you're not meant to. Maybe even start with the rite of hell made flesh, and then come up with some gruesome escape the next time he's come across (this also goes well with the previous point about the ritesmaster's relation with the offender)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7244-innocent-flower","name":"Innocent Flower","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7244_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"322"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-04T08:16:58-07:00","id":859015,"title":"","content":"As far as wording goes, I find this Rite is among the good ones....<br /> <br /> As far as punishment rites goes, WtA is flawed. It lacks punishment for lesser offences, like theft. Also, all Punishment Rites should allow for loss of permanent Renown and Rank. It often doesn't suit the mood to do this by mocking the offending deed, like the Punishment Rite demands.<br /> <br /> But the vengeful teeth is among the three Rites that basically ensure the death of the offender, and in this case even paired with removal from all written history, and turning the name into a curse word/expression. It's not for your garden-variety treason, but for the worst of the worst garou. How they became that bad, without anyone noticing (sense wyrm, anyone?) eludes me, but especially earlier novels/short stories had traitors amongst the garou and they kind of manage.<br /> <br /> If a Ritemaster wants the garou to have a chance, or the truthcatcher, there is the Hunt. The headstart the offender gets can very easily vary depending on how bad one wants the offender to die or get away, in which case the punishment is banishment, for which oddly enough no Rite is existent besides banishment from tribe.<br /> <br /> Sure, there are always instances, where the need of the story trumps the Setting, but aside from these, the Rite is supposed to be a rare occurrence to begin with and a really fatal and unforgiving fate for an ultimately despised offender. So even a former friend, like the Ritemaster, would not want to go easy on a garou who is subject to this Rite (unless a traitor himself).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-04T09:02:54-07:00","id":859048,"title":"","content":"Yes, it's poorly worded.<br /> <br /> Heinrich: My basic hypothesis is (based on the creation-legend of Garou), that everything is made of Gaia.<br /> <br /> The cause of death in silver cloud aspiration wouldn't be suffocation, but a big, bloody, oedema &amp; inflamation.<br /> (The Garou can hold their breath for a loooooong time.)<br /> <br /> <br /> Flower (If I can call you that way. Innocence is always lost.): If your player deserves this Rite, they should be dead. If not by the Rite, the whole Nation should knock their door next morning. If they don't deserve it, the Rite should not be empowered by the Spirits.<br /> If they have a plan to avoid the casting of the Rite on them, it's great, but it not equals with circumventing the Rite's effect.<br /> <br /> By the way, the Hell Made Flesh Rite could be circumvented if the Garou a little bit more than just a shapechanger.: a fomor without skeleton.<br /> <br /> <br /> I think, you should understand (again as my interpretation), that he Punishment Rites is not something the archenemy throws around. Even the name suggests, they are punishments for treason, violaton of laws, unfaithfulness, etc. You CAN'T be punished when you are not guilty (at least when the Spirits are whom empower the Rite). And if they empower it, they shouldn't survive.<br /> <br /> <br /> But I think I have a valiable solution for your Story-Arch (and if you're a Storyteller do as you wish, but don't be inconsistent, it will ruin your World):<br /> The aforementioned &quot;badguy&quot;is tainted by the Wyrm. He thinks, he works in according to the Lithany, but his perception is flawed. They get the caracters, does the Rite, which will work, he belives.<br /> Not the Gaian Spirits, but Banes empower the Rite, but they can't corrupt it totally, this is why there's a slim chance that the characters can survive.<br /> The Nation uproars, because surviving this Rite is unheard so far &amp; they send in the hounds (, Ahrouns &amp; some Ragabash with Sense of the Prey Gift).<br /> To survive &amp; absolve themselves the characters have to prove that they are not guilty &amp; the Wyrm taint of the &quot;badguy&quot;.<br /> Happy End with tons of Renown, chicks and boose.<br /> <br /> Does this make sense to you?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/562-lachdanan","name":"Lachdanan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar562_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-04T13:33:58-07:00","id":859226,"title":"","content":"The more I read this, the more I see that you don't get the point, Flower. The rite is special, unique... the single harshest punishment known to the Garou. It requires special circumstances and a dedicated group of well trained ritualists to perform. The point of it is that the target dies. It's kinda like complaining about Gilgul.<br /> <br /> If you truly need a rite to craft a story around, then pick another one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":1182,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","user":"Asmodai","date":". 04-04-2016, 04:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-04T13:56:02-07:00","id":859237,"title":"","content":"I think it is pretty clear when the rite describes anything of Gaia turning to jagged silver, that doesn't include the air or the Garou itself; if it were so, the rite would say 'Garou turns to silver and dies' or 'air turns to silver and they die.' The idea is that the Earth, Mother Earth, is rejecting one of Her own as punishment for hideous actions. If you want to extrapolate that as a storyteller, go ahead, but it doesn't really fit well with the spirit of the rite.<br /> <br /> If a creative and guilty Garou does try to helicopter away using Dark Aerie or something similar... perhaps then Gaia might will the wind to become silver, just to drive home that none escape Her justice.<br /> <br /> As for the rite of Hell Made Flesh failing due to lack of bones... mental gymnastics aside, this would just be like when an execution fails in real life.<br /> 'Huh, that didn't work. Better try it again using a different method.'<br /> The mockery gets a cute little 'gotcha' moment, mugs for the camera, and then suffers a messy death administered by Gaia's chosen.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3695,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","user":"The Laughing Stranger","date":". 04-04-2016, 05:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-04T14:07:24-07:00","id":859244,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/857464-punishment-rights-and-you?p=859226#post859226\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The more I read this, the more I see that you don't get the point, Flower. The rite is special, unique... the single harshest punishment known to the Garou. It requires special circumstances and a dedicated group of well trained ritualists to perform. The point of it is that the target dies. It's kinda like complaining about Gilgul.<br /> <br /> If you truly need a rite to craft a story around, then pick another one.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think you get the point.<br /> <br /> Gilgul is an execution. Poof,Bang, Avatar destroyed. It's single purpose is to destroy the avatar.<br /> <br /> Gaia's vengeful teeth is more than that. It's not a straight up kill, it's got far more in common with the hunt than it does with the rite of silver death. You're setting up Unfavourable, horrific and humiliating conditions; But you're still sending a pack of crinos out to kill the guy.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> (laughing stranger- Fake it,play dead, but I think that's how things should go. Execution doesn't work? Different execution!)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":7244,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7244-innocent-flower","user":"Innocent Flower","date":". 04-04-2016, 05:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7244-innocent-flower","name":"Innocent Flower","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7244_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"322"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-04T14:30:50-07:00","id":859251,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Innocent Flower</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/857464-punishment-rights-and-you?p=859244#post859244\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think you get the point.<br /> <br /> Gilgul is an execution. Poof,Bang, Avatar destroyed. It's single purpose is to destroy the avatar.<br /> <br /> Gaia's vengeful teeth is more than that. It's not a straight up kill, it's got far more in common with the hunt than it does with the rite of silver death. You're setting up Unfavourable, horrific and humiliating conditions; But you're still sending a pack of crinos out to kill the guy.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> (laughing stranger- Fake it,play dead, but I think that's how things should go. Execution doesn't work? Different execution!)</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure, because its the message. Be a monstrous traitor, and Gaia and her garou will hunt you and kill you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-04T14:30:54-07:00","id":859252,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Innocent Flower</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/857464-punishment-rights-and-you?p=859244#post859244\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think you get the point.<br /> <br /> Gilgul is an execution. Poof,Bang, Avatar destroyed. It's single purpose is to destroy the avatar.<br /> <br /> Gaia's vengeful teeth is more than that. It's not a straight up kill, it's got far more in common with the hunt than it does with the rite of silver death. You're setting up Unfavourable, horrific and humiliating conditions; But you're still sending a pack of crinos out to kill the guy.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's sad when the symbolism of all of Gaia turning away from you and trying to murder you, while your own kind gets to make a sacred hunt on you escapes someone.<br /> I would have thought the idea was quite on the nose.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-04T15:15:39-07:00","id":859285,"title":"","content":"If all gaia turning on you was a serious issue, then the wyrm would never have been a threat. Gaia is fallible. <br /> <br /> The hunt is going to be a harrowing experience, and that's the point. But does harrowing lead to death? No. Some might give up and die, some might beg for forgiveness, but some are going to want to escape and fight back and mechanics wise, there's still precedent for this. Give yourself high willpower and some conviction, or maybe just some wyrm-maddened hate, and you can tell the symbolism to go fuck itself. You're not dying here, and if you're not making a mess now, you can come back for revenge.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7244-innocent-flower","name":"Innocent Flower","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7244_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"322"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-04T16:30:18-07:00","id":859318,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>heinrich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/857464-punishment-rights-and-you?p=858954#post858954\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Martin, the new Lead Storyteller at White Wolf, recently said something about the WoD being realistic in contrast to fantasy settings. While wondering how Mage and Changeling would be non-fantastic, I think it going a bit far if one attributes the Rites to-silver-transmutation property to air or bodily emanations.</div> </div> </div> </div>He's said a lot of things. As before, this one doesn't really explain much, unless you know exactly what he meant by &quot;realistic&quot;, which has to be just unrealistic enough to have werewolves running around, often through the world's soul.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-05T00:34:56-07:00","id":859514,"title":"","content":"Again, below my thoughts you can find.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Innocent Flower</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/857464-punishment-rights-and-you?p=859285#post859285\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If all gaia turning on you was a serious issue, then the wyrm would never have been a threat. Gaia is fallible.<br /> <br /> <b>Take a woman, she is 55 years old, a little crippled &amp; makes good booze. She have 3 sons &amp; tons of chihuahuas</b><b>. One of the boys a little handicapped &amp; he sits in the backyard. The two others are alcoholic. One day the kind mother doesn't give the boose to the boys, because she thinks they need help. The bad boys hit her really hard &amp; lock her in the closet with some of the dogs. The dogs get agitated, because they find a rat &amp; start barking. Can the mother smash a rat with a broomstick?</b><br /> <br /> The hunt is going to be a harrowing experience, and that's the point. But does harrowing lead to death? No. Some might give up and die, some might beg for forgiveness, but some are going to want to escape and fight back and mechanics wise, there's still precedent for this. Give yourself high willpower and some conviction, or maybe just some wyrm-maddened hate, and you can tell the symbolism to go fuck itself. You're not dying here, and if you're not making a mess now, you can come back for revenge.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think you would like to use the Rites for something they are not able. What happens if you throw holy water into an inquisitor face? She gets wet. (Pun intended.)<br /> <br /> You can't punish non-guilty with rites. And maybe Gaia is not able to fight the Triat, it can crush (even just their aspects can) any character.<br /> <br /> <br /> <i>I've got the feeling that you already decided a way to use these Rites &amp; no-one will change your mind. In that case use as you would like, because if you are the ST.<br /> <br /> By the way the WoD have tons of free methods for abusing, from Sulis totem, through the One-Tribe-Rule to the Instruction skill. I don't think you the Rites which should be SACRED in the WW game should be used this way.</i><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/562-lachdanan","name":"Lachdanan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar562_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-05T03:22:31-07:00","id":859537,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/562-lachdanan\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar562_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"562\" data-vbnamecard=\"562\">Lachdanan</a> <br /> If the air was really turning to silver, the garou probably wouldn't be able to hold his breath, since he was having a constant urge to throw up, having his entire throat covered with a layer of silver. Metis will die of agg damage, obviously. Unless Silver Tolerant Merit is in play. Non-metis in breed form will however will suffocate. Sure, an oedema will build and since it is bodily fluid won't turn silver, but it will add to the suffocation not be deadly in it's own right. The same goes for an inflammation.<br /> But that is just my opinion, and air shouldn't turn silver anyways. The logic that it is of Gaia and should therefore turn silver would also be applicable to the sentenced garou and his stomach contents. But, such transmutations in my opinion simply don't fit the mood of the game in general and the Rite in question.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-05T06:50:49-07:00","id":859601,"title":"","content":"The point is the Offender dies. Horribly. If the Offender takes to the sky then that should not be a Get Out of Rite Effect ability, and the air (to the offender) should certainly be as razors of silver. Heck we already have razors of iron and glass in some of the umbral realms forming the winds and the air itself (and you;re being hunted as people say). It's savage, vicious and bloody. There's execution and then there is agonizing, miserable, mystically enforced death.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2767-moirdryd","name":"Moirdryd","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2767_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-05T09:31:23-07:00","id":859694,"title":"","content":"I agree on the death part. Not sure if I'd go the 'the air harms you like razors'-way, though. I mean, how long could he fly or exist without food or drink? Sooner or later, the offender will die - period.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-05T09:33:25-07:00","id":859698,"title":"","content":"Heinrich:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>heinrich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/857464-punishment-rights-and-you?p=859537#post859537\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/562-lachdanan\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar562_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"562\" data-vbnamecard=\"562\">Lachdanan</a><br /> If the air was really turning to silver, the garou probably wouldn't be able to hold his breath, since he was having a constant urge to throw up, having his entire throat covered with a layer of silver. Metis will die of agg damage, obviously. Unless Silver Tolerant Merit is in play. Non-metis in breed form will however will suffocate. Sure, an oedema will build and since it is bodily fluid won't turn silver, but it will add to the suffocation not be deadly in it's own right. The same goes for an inflammation. <b>My basic assumption: small silver splinters would damage the tissues while the body would try to get rid of them - with heavy contractions. The damaged blood vessels would pump the blood into the lung faster then silver could cause fuffocation itself. The pulmonary oedema is when fluid (blood in this case) accumulates in the parenchyma &amp; air spaces, leading to lessened gas exchange &amp; possibly respiratory failure. Yeh, we can say suffocation by your own blood.<br /> <br /> Hey this will be the project of my next PX employee.</b><br /> <br /> But that is just my opinion, and air shouldn't turn silver anyways. The logic that it is of Gaia and should therefore turn silver would also be applicable to the sentenced garou and his stomach contents. But, such transmutations in my opinion simply don't fit the mood of the game in general and the Rite in question.</div> </div> </div> </div>A only mentioned particles of air (fibers, pollens, sand, etc.), hovever, if a ST is too much science-based he could declare even the air (here I mean molecules) could turn to silver &amp; calculate a little. In that case ~25,6 g silver would &quot;come&quot; into it's lungs, if it is in homid form &amp; all of the molecules would hit his surface, assuming the materials would turn to silver in mol to mol basis &amp; not in a weight equivalent basis.<br /> <br /> Hovewer this would couse drastic volume changes...<br /> <br /> <b>What did that lead-ST say about a realistic game?</b><br /> <br /> By the way, kill the subject of this Rite with silver &amp; happy finishy.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/562-lachdanan","name":"Lachdanan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar562_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-05T09:45:02-07:00","id":859705,"title":"","content":"Actually a little surprised everyone's against escaping. <br /> It's like you all hate fun.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7244-innocent-flower","name":"Innocent Flower","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7244_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"322"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-05T10:03:32-07:00","id":859714,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Innocent Flower</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/857464-punishment-rights-and-you?p=859705#post859705\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually a little surprised everyone's against escaping.<br /> It's like you all hate fun.</div> </div> </div> </div>Gaia wept.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-05T12:00:28-07:00","id":859796,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Innocent Flower</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/857464-punishment-rights-and-you?p=859705#post859705\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's like you all hate fun.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's like... you don't want to have a conversation!<br /> <br /> We love fun. I'd wager though, that most of us have fun keeping to the spirit of the game rather than trying to find mechanical loopholes to subvert the spirit of the experience.<br /> <br /> Escaping Gaia's Vengeful Teeth is tossing out the spirit of the game for why that Rite would ever be used; which is unfun.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-05T13:13:30-07:00","id":859825,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Innocent Flower</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/857464-punishment-rights-and-you?p=859705#post859705\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually a little surprised everyone's against escaping.<br /> It's like you all hate fun.</div> </div> </div> </div>Considering -who- the rite is to be used against, is escaping really something you want to see? This Rite is for basically mass murderers, rapists, willingly awful people who by all rights should have Danced the Spiral. It's not something used lightly for a reason.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-06T19:40:57-07:00","id":860729,"title":"","content":"As a long time Philodox player. OP forgets one major bit of information when enacting a punishment rite. If you are violating the contract with the spirits and misusing rituals in such a manner it will bite you in the ass. Your Sept will come down on you, the spirits will come down on you, even your pack, pack totem, and tribe totem will come down on you. You will find yourself in a world of shame even the lowliest BSD will look like a hero compared to you.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1250-shadowlost","name":"Shadowlost","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1250_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"155"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-09T08:16:03-07:00","id":862585,"title":"","content":"Oh a question on Punishment rites? &quot;Rend the Veil, &quot;<br /> <br /> It burns away the Delerium, how is this a punishment in particular, is it because they cant find refuge in madness? <br /> <br /> sorry I just found it confusing...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-09T10:36:28-07:00","id":862648,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/857464-punishment-rights-and-you?p=862585#post862585\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh a question on Punishment rites? &quot;Rend the Veil, &quot;<br /> <br /> It burns away the Delerium, how is this a punishment in particular, is it because they cant find refuge in madness?<br /> <br /> sorry I just found it confusing...</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, it is terrifying... but I figure the poor human will just get killed after learning the truth. It isn't just a messy death, it is one that comes with horrifying clarity. The Garou, inhuman monsters that have stalked the shadows since humanity was in its infancy, want their prey to know that they are dying for sins committed against Gaia.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-09T11:03:56-07:00","id":862662,"title":"","content":"With most senior pentex executives, DNA scientists, you know, those who TRULY deserve this fate, I think we all agree... How to go about getting past their Security... ideas? <br /> <br /> It seems like a fun thing to play through, though its a bit &quot;Beast&quot; ish I know.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-11T01:54:20-07:00","id":863532,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/857464-punishment-rights-and-you?p=862585#post862585\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh a question on Punishment rites? &quot;Rend the Veil, &quot;<br /> It burns away the Delerium, how is this a punishment in particular, is it because they cant find refuge in madness?</div> </div> </div> </div>I, too, find that Rite somewhat critical, by it's implications, but not all garou are Children of Gaia and being cruel as a punishment seems fitting for some tribes...<br /> <br /> But, my guess is, that without the Delirium (and the Veil) the victim can't rationalise away what he sees anymore, and therefore is more likely to go mad. Since madness is usually considered to be of the Wyrm, this whole action seems to help the Wyrm, which is why I think it is a problematic to use.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-11T05:32:29-07:00","id":863578,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>heinrich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/857464-punishment-rights-and-you?p=863532#post863532\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Since madness is usually considered to be of the Wyrm,...</div> </div> </div> </div>Nay, it depends on the type of madness. Wyld taint can also make you mad (Ratkins, anybody?). Check the book of the Wyld. It has plenty of derangements to live with.<br /> <br /> And I belive some types (for example: Obsession: Housecleaning) could be attributed as a Weaver taint.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/562-lachdanan","name":"Lachdanan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar562_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-11T07:48:32-07:00","id":863641,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lachdanan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/857464-punishment-rights-and-you?p=863578#post863578\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Nay, it depends on the type of madness. Wyld taint can also make you mad (Ratkins, anybody?). Check the book of the Wyld. It has plenty of derangements to live with.<br /> <br /> And I belive some types (for example: Obsession: Housecleaning) could be attributed as a Weaver taint.</div> </div> </div> </div>Better to say that it can occasionally feed Triatic spirits, but otherwise has nothing to actually do with them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}